1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,520
Welcome to this short lesson on photosynthesis.

2
00:00:03,520 --> 00:00:09,920
Photosynthesis is the process plants use to turn light energy into chemical energy stored in sugar.

3
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:16,800
It takes place inside the chloroplasts, which are small structures found mostly in the cells of leaves.

4
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:20,800
Chloroplasts contain a green pigment called chlorophyll.

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,800
Chlorophyll absorbs red and blue light and reflects green light, which is why leaves look green.

6
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,920
Photosynthesis happens in two stages.

7
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:33,680
The first stage is called the light-dependent reactions.

8
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:37,120
These take place in the thylacoid membranes.

9
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:41,440
Here, light energy is used to split water molecules.

10
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:47,360
Splitting water releases oxygen as a byproduct, and that is the oxygen we breathe.

11
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:54,800
The energy captured in the stages stored in two carrier molecules, called ATP and NADPH.

12
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,160
The second stage is called the Calvin cycle.

13
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:03,120
It takes place in the stroma, the fluid that surrounds the thylacoids.

14
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:06,480
The Calvin cycle does not need light directly.

15
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:15,200
Instead, it uses the ATP and NADPH made in the first stage to convert carbon dioxide from the air into glucose.

16
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:21,440
So the first stage captures energy, and the second stage uses that energy to build sugar.

17
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:28,240
Three things can limit the rate of photosynthesis, light intensity, carbon dioxide concentration,

18
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,840
and temperature.

19
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:34,320
If any one of them is in short supply, it becomes the limiting factor,

20
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:38,640
and increasing the others will not make photosynthesis go faster.

21
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:44,080
For example, on a bright but very cold day, temperature is the limiting factor,

22
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:48,320
because the enzymes of the Calvin cycle work slowly in the cold.

23
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:54,800
To summarize, plants take in water and carbon dioxide, use light energy to make glucose,

24
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,960
and release oxygen.

25
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:58,960
Thank you for watching.
